 paper_safe='''# Paper-safe claims\n\n## A. SAFE TO SAY\n\n- Frozen Detector v1 detected all 30 evaluated Class-3 events under the stated primary rule.\n- The detector detected 40 of 170 predetermined label-negative/unlabelled control periods.\n- Detector score was strongly associated with channel dimensionality in the examined control population.\n- Class-3 positives were shorter than controls in the evaluated population.\n- Class-3 positives showed a moderate-direction shift toward higher channel counts.\n- The specific hypothesis that the 30/30 result was explained by substantially higher dimensionality among Class-3 positives was weakened, but structural comparability remained limited.\n- These analyses are descriptive and do not establish causation.\n- OPSSAT-AD was used as a protocol/domain stress test rather than direct frozen-v1 validation.\n- The system was demonstrated through actual Yamcs 5.13.2 ground-system integration.\n\n## B. MUST QUALIFY\n\n30/30, 40/170, ROC-AUC 0.9924, the strong-only 1.18% control-detection point, Yamcs 5/6, the OPSSAT result, and all generalization claims. State the population, protocol, denominator, and limitation each time.\n\n## C. MUST NOT SAY\n\n100% accuracy; low or confirmed false-positive rate; broad generalization; OPSSAT validation; operational or flight validation; flight readiness; six-of-six Yamcs equivalence; dimensionality causes false positives; duration causes false positives; or v2 outperforms v1.\n'''
